    21	## What this document is for, and what it is not
    22	
    23	This is the one place an implementer of the V1 verifier or issuer can read what V1 requires. It lists the
    24	requirements, and each one points to where it was decided (source section and rule name; line numbers are
    25	locators only, section 0). Together with A9 and ENCODING-V1 it is intended to be **sufficient with the frozen
    26	catalog, the authenticated trust configuration and the pinned normative dependencies**; those external immutable
    27	inputs do not disappear. [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F17, r2-14.2] *(Dated correction 2026-10-14: previously "each one
    28	points to the line where it was decided"; that overstated it where a requirement points only to a later owner tag.)*
    29	
    30	It is mostly an extraction. Where a rule is already decided, the source is tagged. Where it is not, the gap is
    31	marked `OPEN` and says what must be decided. It also records a small number of **new** choices that no source makes;
    32	each is labelled `OWNER PROFILE DECISION 2026-10-13`, is listed in section 0.1, and is not an A9 citation. It does not restate the byte encoding: for that, read
    33	`formal/p8/ENCODING-V1.md`. It does not hold operating numbers (window dates, stop margins, hardware): those are in
    34	`docs/V1-OPERATIONS-RUNBOOK.md` and are not profile rules. It is not the 2929-line spec, which stays as the design
    35	reference and is synced after V1.
    36	
    37	Where this document and a signed amendment disagree, the amendment wins.
