    96	## 1. Profile identity
    97	
    98	- **Profile id:** `tessera-v1-strict`. It appears in the signed bytes as `common.profile` and in the DNS and git
    99	  record as `profile=`. [ENC §3.2:264; ENC §7:569; A9:142]
   100	- **Spec binding:** `common.spec.id` is `tessera-v1-strict/verification-spec/1` and `common.spec.sha256` is the hash
   101	  of the specification bytes. [ENC §3.2:265-266]
   102	  - `common.spec.id` other than that value gives `INVALID / SPEC_ID`. The verifier compiles in a **frozen spec
   103	    catalog**; a `common.spec.sha256` not in it gives `UNVERIFIABLE / SPEC_UNKNOWN`. The signed `vectors_sha256` and
   104	    `preamble_sha256` must equal the catalog entry (`INVALID / SPEC_OBJECT_MISMATCH`), and the bundled `spec`,
   105	    `vectors`, `preamble` and `dependency_manifest` bytes must hash to their signed or catalog values
   106	    (`INVALID / BUNDLE_OBJECT_HASH`). Bundled objects are hashed, never parsed as policy or executed. The spec and
   107	    vectors objects are assembled by the part format of section 15.8. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G13]
   108	  - **Comparison targets** [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F12]. Bundled spec → signed `common.spec.sha256`; bundled vectors →
   109	    signed `vectors_sha256`; bundled preamble → signed `preamble_sha256`, each independently of catalog lookup
   110	    (`BUNDLE_OBJECT_HASH`). Signed `vectors_sha256` / `preamble_sha256` → catalog entry only if the spec lookup
   111	    succeeds (`SPEC_OBJECT_MISMATCH`). Bundled dependency manifest → catalog entry only if the lookup succeeds;
   112	    otherwise that comparison is unperformable, never compared with an unrelated entry. Other independent failures
   113	    still dominate `SPEC_UNKNOWN`. Bundled objects never become policy because their hashes are self-consistent.
   114	    *(Dated correction 2026-10-14: "must hash to their signed or catalog values" did not say which comparisons
   115	    remain performable for an unknown spec hash.)*
   116	  - **Catalog entry** (one, for V1): the frozen object hashes; exactly one `alg` id (`OPENPGP4-ECDSA-P256-SHA256`
   117	    under the fallback, or the registered pair id under the hybrid); `alg_prohibited` = `[]`; `binding_forms` =
   118	    `["STMT_DIRECT"]`; D, δ, ε, k; the UTC-assessment constants Δ = 7200 s and m = 6 (section 7.4) [OWNER 2026-10-19,
   119	    A10.1.1; A10:284-285; A10 row 22]; DNSSEC algorithms {8, 13} and DS digest types {2, 4}. A well-formed `common.alg`
   120	    other than the catalog id, including the branch not taken, gives `UNVERIFIABLE / ALG_UNKNOWN`. The catalog is
   121	    independent of the bundle and of trust-configuration updates, and later verifiers apply it unchanged to V1
   122	    bundles (A9.4, A9.7 row 29). [OWNER 2026-10-14, G12]
   123	  - **Codec-known versus policy-supported** [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F01]: "Each frame is decoded with E §5.2's codec
   124	    registry, including any authorized supplement, using its own alg and slot. A codec-known but unselected branch
   125	    still uses its specified codec; an id absent from that registry uses the opaque codec. Signature/possession
   126	    verification semantics are performed only for the catalog-supported id. Receipt/manifest alg equality is checked
   127	    independently for every syntactically valid id. M5's catalog-alg condition is performable only for a
   128	    policy-supported id; unsupported ids contribute ALG_UNKNOWN, not an additional SCHEMA failure." The incorporated
   129	    codec baseline and its vectors are unchanged.
   130	  - **Branch-not-taken id before registration.** Until a dated branch-registration supplement registers the hybrid
   131	    pair id, that id (or any stand-in for it) is absent from the codec registry: its frames use the opaque codec and
   132	    the outcome is `UNVERIFIABLE / ALG_UNKNOWN`, with signature and possession semantics unperformable and M5's alg
   133	    condition contributing `ALG_UNKNOWN`, not `SCHEMA`. [OWNER 2026-10-14, codified from diff-1, EA-09]
   134	  - **Baseline.** The governing baseline is the frozen spec object hash in the catalog. A9 incorporates ENCODING-V1 at
   135	    its signing commit; a frozen edited ENCODING-V1 replaces it only with authorized change accounting.
   136	    [OWNER 2026-10-14, G37]
   137	- **Encoding:** `formal/p8/ENCODING-V1.md` at the signing commit, including D-1 to D-17. If the hybrid signer
   138	  branch is taken, the signing-commit baseline plus the dated branch-registration supplement governs. [A9:143-144;
   139	  A9:321-326]
   140	- **Mode:** strict only. One layer. No wrappers, no renewal, no TLR, no waiver policy. `VALID_DEGRADED` is never
   141	  returned. [A9:155; DD:67]
   142	- **Claim and sub-claims:** C1 to C7 as in A9:123-140. This document does not restate them.
