   413	- **Authority: independent release allowlisting** (A9.5 "Trust-configuration authority", OWNER DECISION 2026-10-14).
   414	  The trust configuration is authenticated independently of the bundle and of both authority-channel credentials.
   415	  Each verifier release compiles in the SHA-256 of exactly one trust configuration; the config file itself carries no
   416	  signature. Releases are signed by the **release key**, which neither the DNS credential, the repository key nor the
   417	  issuing AWS account can use; the dated custody record names that key and its access boundary. Capture of any
   418	  authority-channel credential grants no ability to sign a release, authorize a configuration hash, or replace the
   419	  compiled trust root or policy catalog. CI is not the authenticity check. Compromise of the release key is
   420	  distribution compromise, a stated boundary (A9 "The boundaries"). [OWNER 2026-10-14, G08]
