   734	### 6.3 Git channel
   735	
   736	The OTS stamp targets the signed commit's object id, never a tree, blob or unsigned commit. [A9:282-284; ENC
   737	§7.2:685-691] The verifier does four things:
   738	
   739	1. Recomputes the commit id from the presented raw commit object.
   740	2. Verifies `gpgsig` over the object without that header, under the pinned repository key.
   741	3. Follows commit, then tree, then blob, down the fixed path below.
   742	4. Checks that the stamped bytes name that id.
   743	
   744	[ENC §7.2:706-710] SHA-1 linkage (the commit id and the commit-tree-blob links) is a stated residual. [A9:284;
   745	ENC §7.2:712-718]
