  1501	### 15.1 Container [OWNER 2026-10-14, G14, G17, G33]
  1502	
  1503	A bundle is one UTF-8 JSON text that passes ENC §1.4 checks 1–5 and 7 and is canonical JCS. It contains no JSON
  1504	numbers. Heights and durations are decimal strings matching `0|[1-9][0-9]*` with value at most 4294967295. Binary
  1505	values are RFC 4648 §4 base64 with padding that round-trips (no non-zero pad bits, no line breaks). Size cap 2^27
  1506	bytes. Top level: exactly `{"layers":[L],"profile":"tessera-v1-strict"}`. After dispatch (section 3.1): a
  1507	non-canonical container is `INVALID / JSON_NONCANONICAL`; then the absence rule (section 2.1) and A9.5's
  1508	`git.object_format` outcomes; then any other schema failure is `INVALID / CONTAINER_SCHEMA`. Absence is inspected
  1509	only beneath correctly typed parents, a present non-string `object_format` is `CONTAINER_SCHEMA`, and a present
  1510	`issuer_record` with an absent internal field is `CONTAINER_SCHEMA` (section 2.1). [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F03]
  1511	
  1512	**Numbers.** JSON numbers are admitted syntactically at dispatch (D1's strict-JSON checks do not exclude them, and
  1513	D2/D3 read only `profile` and the length of `layers`) and rejected after dispatch by the container schema: a JSON
  1514	number anywhere in the layer is `INVALID / CONTAINER_SCHEMA` (row 2.4, after row 2.1), never `OUT_OF_PROFILE`.
  1515	[OWNER 2026-10-14, codified from diff-1, A10]
  1516	
  1517	Layer `L` (closed; each member exactly once; all values base64 unless marked):
