  1532	### 15.2 OTS proofs and the txid [OWNER 2026-10-14, G20]
  1533	
  1534	OWNER CHOICE (supported-path limit). python-opentimestamps 0.4.5 is the reference reader, not normative.
  1535	- **Header.** Magic `00 4f70656e54696d657374616d7073 0000 50726f6f66 00 bf89e2e884e89294`, varuint major version 1,
  1536	  file-hash op `08` (SHA-256 only), the 32-byte digest, one Timestamp, end of input.
  1537	- **Timestamp.** `Timestamp := (ff Item)* Item`; `Item := 00 Attestation | Op Timestamp`.
  1538	- **Ops.** `08` (sha256), `f0 varbytes` (append), `f1 varbytes` (prepend). Arguments 1–4096 bytes; every message and
  1539	  result at most 4096 bytes.
  1540	- **Attestations.** `tag(8) varbytes(payload)`, payload at most 8192 bytes. Bitcoin `0588960d73d71901`: payload is
  1541	  exactly one varuint height. Pending `83dfe30d2ef90c8e`: payload varbytes(URI ≤ 1000), URI ignored.
  1542	- **Wire completion** [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F09]. `varbytes := varuint byte_count || exactly byte_count octets`.
  1543	  Both the pending and the Bitcoin payloads must be consumed exactly (the pending payload's inner URI framing
  1544	  included); otherwise `OTS_FORMAT`. A Bitcoin attestation whose message is not exactly 32 bytes is `INVALID /
  1545	  OTS_FORMAT`, independently of header availability. Timestamp depth: the root Timestamp has depth 0, each Op →
  1546	  Timestamp step adds 1, `ff` siblings do not add. Op and attestation counts are of serialized items, duplicates
  1547	  included; duplicates are semantically inert only within those limits.
  1548	- **Varuint.** LEB128, shortest form only, value ≤ 2^32 − 1. (python-opentimestamps 0.4.5 accepts redundant groups;
  1549	  V1 does not.)
  1550	- **Bounds.** Depth ≤ 256; ≤ 65536 ops and ≤ 4096 attestations per proof; proof ≤ 2^20 bytes. Duplicate identical
  1551	  branches are permitted and have no effect.
  1552	- **Rejections.** Any other op or tag, or any grammar or bound violation: `INVALID / OTS_FORMAT`. File digest must be
  1553	  SHA256(`A_sig`) for the receipt (`RECEIPT_ANCHOR_MISMATCH`), SHA256 of the ENC §6 envelope for the snapshot
  1554	  (`SNAPSHOT_STAMP_MISMATCH`), SHA256 of `<40-hex commit id>\n` for git (`GIT_STAMP_MISMATCH`).
  1555	- **Merkle link.** A Bitcoin attestation's message is 32 bytes and equals bytes 36–68 of the bundled header at that
  1556	  height.
  1557	- **Header fields** [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F09]. In a raw 80-byte header: prev = `header[4:36]`, merkle root =
  1558	  `header[36:68]`, nTime = `uint32le(header[68:72])`.
  1559	- **txid (supported-proof subset).** On the path to the **selected** attestation, let the first two consecutive
  1560	  sha256 ops have input P, and let m be the message immediately before the maximal run of append/prepend ops that
  1561	  precedes them. Required: (1) P parses exactly, consuming every byte, as a non-witness Bitcoin transaction —
  1562	  version (4), compact-size input count ≥ 1, inputs (32 + 4 + compact-size script length + script + 4), compact-size
  1563	  output count ≥ 1, outputs (8 + compact-size length + script), locktime (4); no SegWit marker; compact sizes
  1564	  shortest form; (2) m is 32 bytes and some output script is exactly `6a 20 ‖ m`; (3) `hex(reverse(SHA256d(P)))`
  1565	  equals `receipt_anchor.txid`. Otherwise `INVALID / ANCHOR_TXID_MISMATCH`. Any one path to the selected height may
  1566	  satisfy this. (All 344 Bitcoin paths in the repository's 127 proofs had this shape when RES G20 was written; the
  1567	later owner check of 2026-10-14 under part (4) below counts 352 paths in 129 proofs, all conforming. Evidence, not a
  1568	rule. [OWNER 2026-10-19, Levadura contested 6])
  1569	- **CompactSize and transaction fields** [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F09]. A first byte < 253 is the value; `fd` then u16le,
  1570	  `fe` then u32le, `ff` then u64le; shortest form only; a length or count exceeding the remaining bytes is rejected
  1571	  before allocation. Version, value and locktime are parsed as their fixed-width bytes (4, 8, 4) and not
  1572	  interpreted. Consensus validity and script execution are supplied by authentic pinned history, not revalidated
  1573	  here.
  1574	- **(4) Merkle suffix (owner choice, fail-closed)** [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F09]. After the two sha256 ops that
  1575	  produce the txid, the path to the selected attestation consists only of zero or more repetitions of (append or
  1576	  prepend of exactly 32 bytes, sha256, sha256); an empty suffix is a one-transaction block. Otherwise `INVALID /
  1577	  ANCHOR_TXID_MISMATCH` for the receipt. Without it, arbitrary allowed operations could follow the identified
  1578	  transaction. All 352 Bitcoin paths in the repository's 129 proofs have this suffix (owner check 2026-10-14;
  1579	  evidence, not a rule). This is a missing structural definition, not a demonstrated forged timestamp.
  1580	- **Scope** [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F08]. Parts (1), (2) and (4) apply at the selected height of the receipt, snapshot
  1581	  and git proofs; part (3), the txid equality, applies to `receipt_anchor` only. Snapshot or git failure of (1), (2)
  1582	  or (4) at every qualifying path at its h*: `INVALID / OTS_TX_SHAPE`. h* is selected first (section 7.1); a failing
  1583	  path never moves selection to a higher height.
