  1585	### 15.3 DNSSEC snapshot body [OWNER 2026-10-14, G19, G24, G30]
  1586	
  1587	A concatenation of RRs, each in RFC 1035 §3.2.1 wire format, uncompressed, in RFC 4034 §6.2 canonical form (owner
  1588	name and every domain-name field inside RDATA, including the RRSIG signer name, lowercase and uncompressed).
  1589	1. **Groups, in order:** the root DNSKEY group; then for each zone z below the root down to the TXT's signer zone, a
  1590	   DS group at z and a DNSKEY group at z; last the TXT group at `_tessera-v1.<D>`. A group is a maximal run of RRs
  1591	   with the same owner, CLASS IN, and TYPE t (the RRset) or TYPE RRSIG with Type Covered t (its witnesses). The RRset
  1592	   comes first, in RFC 4034 §6.3 canonical RDATA order without duplicates, then zero or more RRSIGs in (key tag,
  1593	   inception, expiration, signature bytes) order. Each z is a proper descendant of the previous zone. Signer names:
  1594	   the parent for DS, z for DNSKEY, the root for the root group, the last z for TXT.
  1595	   - **Serialization ties and duplicates** [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F07]. Canonical RRSIG RDATA is the final body
  1596	     serialization sort key: RRSIGs sort by (key tag, inception, expiration, signature bytes, canonical RRSIG
  1597	     RDATA). A duplicate is an RR identical in owner, class, type and RDATA (`SNAPSHOT_FORMAT`); TTL consistency
  1598	     within an RRset is checked separately (point 2).
  1599	   - **Raw time fields in sort keys.** Inception and expiration in these sort keys, and in the G35 candidate tuple
  1600	     (section 7.3), are the raw 32-bit unsigned RRSIG field values compared numerically (equivalently, as
  1601	     big-endian bytes), not the absolute times resolved by section 7.3's serial arithmetic; the two orders differ
  1602	     only across the 2^32 wrap. [OWNER 2026-10-14, codified from diff-1, EA-13]
  1603	   - **Too-short RRSIG.** An RRSIG whose RDATA (within a consistent RDLENGTH) is too short for RFC 4034 §3.1's
  1604	     fixed fields and signer name is attributed to the group of the immediately preceding RRs at the same owner,
  1605	     not treated as a framing failure, and is malformed supported RRSIG RDATA: `INVALID / DNSSEC_FORMAT`
  1606	     (section 6.1). [OWNER 2026-10-14, codified from diff-1, A06]
  1607	   - **Chain skeleton, recovery grammar** [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F06]. The root is the initial zone. The ordered zone
  1608	     skeleton is constructed from the supplied DS and DNSKEY owners and the RRSIG signer names: each names a zone,
  1609	     and the zones, ordered by descent, must form one chain from the root. Omitted DS, DNSKEY, root DNSKEY or TXT
  1610	     groups are admitted as missing evidence (`UNVERIFIABLE / DNS_EVIDENCE_MISSING`; root:
  1611	     `NO_TRUSTED_KSK_USABLE`); omission alone is never a format failure. Direct signing of the TXT by the root, or
  1612	     by any ancestor zone in the skeleton, is permitted (section 6.1 retains ancestor signing authority); "the last
  1613	     z" is the TXT RRSIG's signer zone, which is the root when no below-root zone is supplied. Conflicting supplied
  1614	     transitions or signer names (names not forming one descent chain, a DS group not signed by its parent zone in
  1615	     the skeleton, a DNSKEY group not signed by its own zone, a group after the TXT group) are `INVALID /
  1616	     SNAPSHOT_FORMAT`. A supplied final TXT owner is checked by ENC §7's `DNS_OWNER`, even when wrong; its existence
  1617	     does not itself constitute an "outside-chain" framing failure. *(Dated correction 2026-10-14: the grammar did
  1618	     not say whether a skipped zone was omission or inconsistency, and "the last z" was undefined for a TXT signed
  1619	     by the root.)*
  1620	2. **Fields.** CLASS IN. TTL equal within an RRset and otherwise uninterpreted; validation uses the RRSIG's Original
  1621	   TTL.
  1622	3. **Framing versus completeness.** A truncated RR encoding, forbidden RR type, duplicate RR, inconsistent
  1623	   owner/type within a group, or misordered supplied group is `INVALID / SNAPSHOT_FORMAT`. Among RDATA defects,
  1624	   RR boundary/RDLENGTH truncation and any domain-name field inside RDATA that is not in the canonical form above (an
  1625	   uppercase ASCII letter or a compression pointer, including in the RRSIG signer name) are `INVALID /
  1626	   SNAPSHOT_FORMAT`, whatever other witnesses the body carries; TXT's internal character-string parsing uses ENC's
  1627	   `DNS_RDATA` / `DNS_STRINGS`, and other malformed supported DNSKEY/RRSIG RDATA is `DNSSEC_FORMAT` (section 6.1).
  1628	   [OWNER 2026-10-14, diff-1 F-1: the earlier wording let a non-canonical RRSIG beside a valid witness reach
  1629	   `VALID_STRICT` in one implementation and `INVALID` in another; fail-closed chosen.]
  1630	   A defect in an RR's owner-name wire encoding is `SNAPSHOT_FORMAT`; a defect of the RRSIG signer-name field
  1631	   other than the non-canonical forms just named (which are `SNAPSHOT_FORMAT` under diff-1 F-1) and other than a
  1632	   recovery-grammar conflict is malformed supported RRSIG RDATA, `DNSSEC_FORMAT`. [OWNER 2026-10-14, codified from
  1633	   diff-1, A12]
  1634	   [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F06, r2-F05] A syntactically complete
  1635	   sequence lacking a required RRset or its witness RRSIG is `UNVERIFIABLE / DNS_EVIDENCE_MISSING` (root:
  1636	   `NO_TRUSTED_KSK_USABLE`). Missing groups alone are not order violations. Forbidden: any type other than DNSKEY, DS,
  1637	   TXT and RRSIG, and any RR at a name outside the chain (the final TXT group excepted, see the recovery grammar);
  1638	   CNAME and DNAME are not followed. An empty body is `LENGTH_CAP`.
  1639	4. **Wildcards:** `INVALID / DNS_WILDCARD` (section 6.1). This is the global no-wildcard body restriction: any
  1640	   RRSIG in the body with Labels less than its owner's label count, whatever other witnesses the body carries.
  1641	   [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F07] The Labels octet is read, and this restriction applied, whenever an RRSIG's RDATA
  1642	   has at least 4 bytes (Type Covered, Algorithm, Labels), however malformed the rest of that RDATA is.
  1643	   [OWNER 2026-10-14, codified from diff-1, A07]
  1644	5. **Envelope:** ENC §6, `header ‖ u32 len ‖ body`, 1 ≤ len ≤ 2^24.
