     1	Tessera V1 purpose preamble (profile tessera-v1-strict). This bundle is a Tessera V1 receipt. With the verifier, anyone can check it without Tessera. A VALID_STRICT result shows three things. The content bytes in this bundle were signed by two keys. The DNS record _tessera-v1.wamason.com (DNSSEC) and a signed git commit named those two keys as the keys of the Tessera V1 service. The content and both signatures existed before a named Bitcoin block was mined. If one party took control of both the DNS record and the git signing key, receipts under that party's keys also give VALID_STRICT; this receipt cannot tell them apart. The block's header time T is not a UTC upper bound. A UTC bound is reported only under the stated assumption A-UTC. The receipt does not identify who submitted the content. It does not check the meaning of the content or any signature inside it. It does not check revocation or standing. To check it, use the specification and conformance vectors in this bundle and the standards named in its dependency manifest.
