   347	
   348	**Signer profile, conditional.** The hybrid records the author's stated preference (2026-10-12: *"I think we
   349	should build our V1 with a PQ implementation"*). It is not a claim requirement: no sentence of C1–C7 needs it. It
   350	is the first item cut if 30 Oct slips (A9.2).
   351	- **If the hybrid spike passes by 21 Oct:** slot `kms` is AWS KMS **ML-DSA-65** (FIPS 204, in KMS's HSMs), raw
   352	  signature per ENCODING-V1 §5.2 rule R; slot `gpg` is **P-256** OpenPGP (rule O), signed by a
   353	  non-exportable, hardware-protected key in a separate technical key-custody domain outside the issuing AWS account
   354	  (*slot-2 custody*, below), pulling from a queue with no inbound path.
   355	  One pair algorithm identifier names both slot schemes (`common.alg` is shared, R-3.12). This adopts for V1 the
   356	  hybrid A3 §A3.6 deferred.
